# /etc/sudoers.d/station-netwatch -- the station Wi-Fi watchdog's root
# actions (issue #686), and nothing else. A TEMPLATE: Servers/install-netwatch.sh
# replaces WIFI_IFACE with this station's interface (wlx + the stick's MAC),
# checks the result with visudo and installs it. Don't copy this file by hand.
#
# Exact names, no wildcards: the stations run sudo-rs (Ubuntu 26.04's sudo),
# which rejects wildcards in command arguments. If the stick is swapped, its
# interface name changes: re-run the installer. Until then, rungs 1 and 2 log
# a sudo error and the reboot rung still works.
#
# Why sudo lines and not a root unit: todd's sudo asks for a password, and
# flyway/netwatch.py lives in the todd-owned checkout that station-autodeploy
# updates from GitHub. A root unit would run that tree as root every two
# minutes -- a new todd-to-root path. These lines grant only: bounce the Wi-Fi
# device, unbind/bind a USB device, reboot. No other file writes, no shell.
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/nmcli device disconnect WIFI_IFACE
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/nmcli device connect WIFI_IFACE
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tee /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usb/unbind
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/tee /sys/bus/usb/drivers/usb/bind
todd ALL=(root) NOPASSWD: /usr/bin/systemctl reboot
